headers {
  accept: application/json
  content-type: application/json
}

auth {
  mode: none
}

vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://localhost:8080/
  v1Path: api/v1
  v2Path: api/v2
  adminUsername: admin
  adminPassword: 123456
  userUsername: student
  userPassword: 123456
}

docs {
  # PRN232 LMS API
  
  Bruno collection for the Lab 02 PRN232 LMS API.
  
  ## Quick start
  1. Pick the `Local` env (top-right).
  2. Run `Auth → Login` to obtain a token. The script stores `accessToken` / `refreshToken` in the active env.
  3. Hit any other request — they read the bearer token automatically.
  
  ## Roles
  - `admin` / `123456` — Admin role, full access.
  - `student` / `123456` — User role, gets 403 on `AdminOnly` endpoints (use `Auth → Login - Student` to swap).
  
  ## Versioning
  - `v1/` uses `/api/v1` routes.
  - `v2/` uses `/api/v2` routes (extra `phoneNumber`, `studentCode` fields).
  
  ## Notes
  - `Create *` requests auto-save the new id into the env so PUT/DELETE chain works.
  - `Subjects → Get Subject - XML` and `Subjects → Get Subject - 406 Unsupported` cover content negotiation.
  - Credentials live as collection vars; `Local` env can override per env.
}
